INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers") VALUES (4600971931020125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Importance of Chemistry in “Basic Concepts of Chemistry”. Define the concept, describe the main principles or steps, and give an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain tetravalency of carbon in “General Organic Chemistry”. Define the concept, describe the main principles or steps, and give an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Types of electrochemical cells and examples in “Electromotive Force”. Define the concept, describe the main principles or steps, and give an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain classification of polymers in “Polymers”. Define the concept, describe the main principles or steps, and give an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** Importance of Chemistry is covered in “Basic Concepts of Chemistry”. Define its purpose, explain the main steps or components, relate it to Nature of matter, classification based on physical state, classification based on chemical structure, Physical quantities, give a practical example, and state one check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to Nature of matter, classification based on physical state, classification based on chemical structure, Physical quantities. State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical APPLIED CHEMISTRY task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** tetravalency of carbon is covered in “General Organic Chemistry”. Define its purpose, explain the main steps or components, relate it to hybridization, sp2 and sp3 hybrid orbitals with examples, functional groups, IUPAC nomenclature of organic compounds, give a practical example, and state one check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to hybridization, sp2 and sp3 hybrid orbitals with examples, functional groups, IUPAC nomenclature of organic compounds. State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical APPLIED CHEMISTRY task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** Types of electrochemical cells and examples is covered in “Electromotive Force”. Define its purpose, explain the main steps or components, relate it to Half- cell, Reversible and irreversible cell, Convention sign, Types of electrodes, give a practical example, and state one check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to Half- cell, Reversible and irreversible cell, Convention sign, Types of electrodes. State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical APPLIED CHEMISTRY task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** Polymers contain repeating units; properties depend on monomer chemistry, chain structure and processing.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to industrial manufacturing, properties and uses of some important polymers: Polythene, Teflon, Polyacrylonitrile. State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** A