INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers") VALUES (4600991101010132, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical BHARATIYA KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM task within “Science and Mathematics in Ancient Bharat”, the requirement is the function or principle associated with Indian Language Sciences (Components of a Language. Explain how Indian Language Sciences (Components of a Language applies and justify the method with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical BHARATIYA KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM task within “Engineering, Technology and Architecture in Ancient Bharat”, the requirement is the function or principle associated with Metallurgy and Textile Technology (Metals and Metalworking Technology. Explain how Metallurgy and Textile Technology (Metals and Metalworking Technology applies and justify the method with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical BHARATIYA KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM task within “Concepts of Life in Ancient Bharat”, the requirement is the function or principle associated with Four Stages of Life. Explain how Four Stages of Life applies and justify the method with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical BHARATIYA KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM task within “Introduction to Bharatiya Knowledge Systems (BKS)”, the requirement is the function or principle associated with The Vedic Corps & Philosophical Systems (Introduction to the Four Vedas. Explain how The Vedic Corps & Philosophical Systems (Introduction to the Four Vedas applies and justify the method with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** Indian Language Sciences (Components of a Language is covered in “Science and Mathematics in Ancient Bharat”. Define its purpose, explain the main steps or components, relate it to Sanskrit and Role of Sanskrit in Natural Language Processing), Number System and Units of Measurement (Number System in India – Historical Evidence, Measurement for Time, Distance and Weight), give a practical example, and state one check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to Sanskrit and Role of Sanskrit in Natural Language Processing), Number System and Units of Measurement (Number System in India – Historical Evidence, Measurement for Time, Distance and Weight). State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical BHARATIYA KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** Metallurgy and Textile Technology (Metals and Metalworking Technology is covered in “Engineering, Technology and Architecture in Ancient Bharat”. Define its purpose, explain the main steps or components, relate it to Iron and Steel Technology, Textile and Dyeing – Indian Specialities), Irrigation and Water Management (Harappan and Traditional Water Management System of Gujarat, Historical Sites – Sringeverpur, give a practical example, and state one check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to Iron and Steel Technology, Textile and Dyeing – Indian Specialities), Irrigation and Water Management (Harappan and Traditional Water Management System of Gujarat, Historical Sites – Sringeverpur. State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical BHARATIYA KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** Four Stages of Life is covered in “Concepts of Life in Ancient Bharat”. Define its purpose, explain the main steps or components, relate it to Four Goals of Human Life, Karma & Rebirth, Striving for Moksha, Concepts of Life in Ancient Bharat, give a practical example, and state one check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to Four Goals of Human Life, Karma & Rebirth, Striving for Moksha, Concepts of Life in Ancient Bharat. State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical BHARATIYA KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** The Vedic Corps & Philosophical Systems (Introduction to the Four Vedas is covered in “Introduction to Bharatiya Knowledge Systems (BKS)”. Define its purpose, explain the main steps or components, relate it to Definition and classification of BKS, Caturdasa-Vidyasthana, Vedangas, Vedic School of Philosophy), give a practical example, and state one check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to Definition and classification of BKS, Caturdasa-Vidyasthana, Vedangas, Vedic School of Philosophy). State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical BHARATIYA KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

-- BHARATIYA KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM | ESE | hard | reused-existing-bank | 4600991101010133
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers") VALUES (4600991101010133, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving metallurgy and iron/steel technology in historical india, such as evaluating an artifact or historical description of iron production. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving traditional textile technology and dyeing, such as describing how a natural dye process moves from source material to finished cloth. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving water management and rainwater harvesting, such as planning a system for collecting seasonal rainfall in a settlement. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic problem involving sacred ecology, forests and agricultural knowledge, such as assessing a claim connecting seasonal observations with farm decisions. Present a reasoned approach, justify key decisions, and state an important limitation or verification check."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer:\nMetallurgy includes obtaining metals from ores and shaping or treating them for use. A historical discussion can cover ore preparation, heating and reduction, forging, joining, heat treatment and the properties sought, while recognizing that techniques varied across periods and regions. Iron and steel production requires evidence about the artifact, process and material; the existence of a notable artifact does not prove that one technique was universal. A well-supported answer connects process to properties such as strength, hardness, corrosion behaviour or workability and identifies the limits of the available evidence.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nTextile technology includes fibre preparation, spinning, weaving and finishing. Dyeing adds colour using a dye source and a process suited to the fibre; preparation, temperature, time and mordants can affect shade and colour fastness. Historical Indian textile traditions included sophisticated regional practices, but materials and techniques differed. To analyze a process, identify the fibre, colour source, preparation, application and finishing steps, then explain how these steps influence the result. Avoid treating all traditional dyes or textile methods as chemically or historically identical.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nWater management combines collection, storage, distribution, drainage and maintenance. Rainwater harvesting captures runoff from a roof or catchment, conveys it through channels, filters or settles sediment, and stores or recharges it where appropriate. Traditional systems were adapted to local rainfall, terrain, materials and community needs; Gujarat and other regions contain different examples. A useful analysis checks catchment area, water demand, overflow, contamination prevention and maintenance responsibility. Historical systems should be explained in their local setting rather than assumed to work unchanged in every modern site.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nTraditional ecological knowledge may connect land, water, forests, seasonal cycles and social or religious practices. A study of Nakshatra-related agricultural knowledge should identify the particular calendar or observational claim and compare it with the local context and available evidence. Forest management and sacred natural sites can also be studied for their cultural meaning and practical conservation effects. Do not assume that every community followed one identical practice or that cultural association alone proves a measurable ecological outcome. Distinguish historical description, current practice and independently tested environmental effects.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should explain the governing concept, justify the chosen method, check the result and acknowledge a relevant limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

