INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers") VALUES (460009382101011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Basic chemical engineering symbols in “Various laboratory equipment and devices”. Define the concept, describe the main principles or steps, and give an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Basic of block diagram and flow diagram of chemical process industries in “Block Diagram and Flow diagram”. Define the concept, describe the main principles or steps, and give an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Types of storage vessel and pressure vessel in detail in “Storage vessels and Pressure vessel”. Define the concept, describe the main principles or steps, and give an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Types of reaction vessel in detail in “Reaction Vessel”. Define the concept, describe the main principles or steps, and give an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** Basic chemical engineering symbols is covered in “Various laboratory equipment and devices”. Define its purpose, explain the main steps or components, relate it to Laboratory glass ware, instruments and their practice, Various laboratory equipment and devices, give a practical example, and state one check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to Laboratory glass ware, instruments and their practice, Various laboratory equipment and devices. State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical CHEMICAL ENGINEERING EQUIPMENT DESIGN task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** Basic of block diagram and flow diagram of chemical process industries is covered in “Block Diagram and Flow diagram”. Define its purpose, explain the main steps or components, relate it to Block Diagram and Flow diagram, give a practical example, and state one check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to Block Diagram and Flow diagram. State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical CHEMICAL ENGINEERING EQUIPMENT DESIGN task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** A pressure vessel contains fluid at design pressure and temperature; design considers allowable stress, joints, corrosion allowance, supports and applicable codes.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to Heads, Covers, and Supports, Storage vessels and Pressure vessel. State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical CHEMICAL ENGINEERING EQUIPMENT DESIGN task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** Types of reaction vessel in detail is covered in “Reaction Vessel”. Define its purpose, explain the main steps or components, relate it to glass line reactor jacketed reactor etc, and different parts of reactor vessel, Reaction Vessel, give a practical example, and state one check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to glass line reactor jacketed reactor etc, and different parts of reactor vessel, Reaction Vessel. State relevant condit