ion/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** Skimming finds the main idea, scanning searches for a specific detail, and intensive reading supports close comprehension.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to Reading & Structure (Tenses, Parts of Speech, Subject-Verb Agreement, Modals. State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical COMMUNICATION SKILLS task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2):** Skimming finds the main idea, scanning searches for a specific detail, and intensive reading supports close comprehension.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept in sequence and connect it to Reading & Structure (Tenses, Parts of Speech, Types of Sentences, Subject-Verb Agreement. State relevant conditions, components or formulas.\n\n**Application (2):** Apply it to a practical COMMUNICATION SKILLS task and state the expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result against the requirement and state a limitation, risk or error source.\n\nMarking guide: definition 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

-- COMMUNICATION SKILLS | ESE | medium | reused-existing-bank | 4609191201030129
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers") VALUES (4609191201030129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A student must apply planning and writing a clear formal email in a practical situation such as requesting a meeting with a faculty member about a lab submission. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply structure and tone of a formal application in a practical situation such as applying for permission to attend an academic event. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply writing an event or industrial-visit report in a practical situation such as reporting a college visit with observations and outcomes. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply planning and organizing an assignment in a practical situation such as turning a broad topic into a well-structured short assignment. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer:\nA formal email needs a specific subject line, an appropriate greeting, a concise opening that states the purpose, organized details, a clear request or next step, a courteous closing and the sender''s name. Use a professional tone, correct grammar and paragraphs that each serve one purpose. Check the recipient address and any attachment before sending. Add CC only for people who need visibility and BCC when recipients should not see one another''s addresses. Do not place confidential information in unnecessary recipients or subject lines.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA formal application identifies the recipient, date, subject and applicant, then states the request clearly and gives only relevant reasons or supporting details. It uses a respectful salutation, concise body paragraphs, a clear closing and the required signature or identification. The writer should maintain a formal tone, avoid slang and emotional exaggeration, and ensure the requested action is explicit. Proofread names, dates and attachments. A good application lets the recipient understand what is being requested, why it is justified and what response or approval is needed.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA report records an event objectively and in a structured order. Include a meaningful title, date and place, purpose, participants, major activities, observations, outcomes and a conclusion or recommendations where appropriate. Arrange events chronologically or under clear headings and use past tense for completed activities. Separate observed facts from personal opinion and support claims with reliable details. Proofread names and dates, keep the language concise, and make the report useful to a reader who did not attend the event.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nBegin by interpreting the task and identifying the expected scope. Gather relevant sources, make an outline, and organize the introduction, main discussion and conclusion in a logical sequence. Each paragraph should develop one idea and connect it to the overall argument. Use accurate examples and acknowledge sources in the required format; do not copy text without attribution. Revise for completeness, flow, factual accuracy and grammar, then check formatting and submission requirements. A strong assignment answers the exact question rather than merely collecting loosely related information.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

